 "text": {
  "what": "The Christian charitable organisation whose World War I canteens fried donuts for American soldiers, and whose Chicago branch created National Donut Day in 1938.",
  "story": "The 1938 day was a Depression fundraiser: money for people in need, and recognition for the Lassies of 1917 and 1918.",
  "today": "Donut shops across the country still give donuts away on the first Friday in June, mostly without mentioning the fundraiser."
 },
